INT. MORDECAI'S PAWN SHOP - CLOSING SALE - NIGHT

Shelves of guitars, watches, tuba cases. A red banner: EVERYTHING MUST GO.

PAWNBROKER MORDECAI, 60s, cash apron, stands behind the counter. GINA, 30s, a regular, waves a ticket at him. TREY, 20s, a skinny kid in a hoodie, edges toward the display case. ROSALIND, 40s, a plainclothes cop, pretends to look at saxophones. DUKE, 50s, a large man in a leather vest, blocks the door.

MORDECAI
We're closed!

GINA
The banner says sale!

TREY
I just want the ring.

ROSALIND
Which ring?

TREY
The one in the case.

DUKE
Nobody leaves.

MORDECAI
Nobody enters, Duke! We're closed!

GINA
Mordecai, my grandmother's locket --

TREY
It's not for sale, it's for me --

MORDECAI
Everybody shut up!

Silence. Then Rosalind flashes her badge.

ROSALIND
Police. Everybody hands up.

Mordecai lifts his hands. Gina lifts her ticket. Trey lunges for the case. Duke steps aside to let Rosalind through.

MORDECAI
Duke!

GINA
(overlapping)
TREY!

DUKE
(simultaneously)
She's a cop!

Trey smashes the glass. Grabs the ring. Bolts.

ROSALIND
(over her shoulder)
Duke, stop him!

Duke grins and sits down on the nearest tuba case.
